---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import LegalIntro from '../components/LegalIntro.astro';
import Fact from '../components/Fact.astro';
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'provider', label: '1. Provider and effective date' },
  { id: 'service', label: '2. The service and eligibility' },
  { id: 'accounts', label: '3. Accounts' },
  { id: 'responsibilities', label: '4. Your responsibilities' },
  { id: 'acceptable-use', label: '5. Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'meta', label: '6. Facebook and Instagram' },
  { id: 'ai', label: '7. AI-generated responses' },
  { id: 'payment', label: '8. Payment and cancellation' },
  { id: 'availability', label: '9. Availability' },
  { id: 'ip', label: '10. Intellectual property' },
  { id: 'data', label: '11. Confidentiality and your data' },
  { id: 'termination', label: '12. Suspension and termination' },
  { id: 'liability', label: '13. Liability and governing law' },
  { id: 'complaints', label: '14. Complaints and disputes' },
];
---

<DocLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that apply when a business uses Get Assist, including Facebook and Instagram connections, AI-generated replies, payment and termination."
  toc={toc}
>
  <div slot="intro">
    <LegalIntro title="Terms of Service">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Summary in plain language</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate">
        <li>These terms apply to businesses that use {site.brand}.</li>
        <li>
          You are responsible for the Pages and accounts you connect and for how you use them with
          your customers.
        </li>
        <li>
          AI replies can be wrong. You decide whether they are sent automatically or reviewed.
        </li>
        <li>Your conversation data belongs to you, and you can export or delete it.</li>
      </ul>
    </LegalIntro>
  </div>

  <h2 id="provider">1. Provider and effective date</h2>
  <p>
    {site.brand} is provided by <Fact fact={site.operator.legalName} />,{' '}
    <Fact fact={site.operator.address} />, <Fact fact={site.operator.country} /> (“we”, “us”). These
    terms take effect on <Fact fact={site.legal.effectiveDate} />.
  </p>

  <h2 id="service">2. The service and eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    {site.brand} lets a business receive and answer Facebook Messenger and Instagram direct messages
    in one inbox, with AI-assisted replies based on a knowledge base the business provides and
    handover to people on its team. Features and their current status are listed on the{' '}
    <a href="/features">features page</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Who may use the service: <Fact fact={site.legal.eligibility} />
  </p>

  <h2 id="accounts">3. Accounts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Give accurate information when you create an account and keep it up to date.</li>
    <li>Keep your sign-in details secret. You are responsible for activity under your account.</li>
    <li>You may invite teammates; you are responsible for what they do in your account.</li>
    <li>
      Tell us straight away at <EmailLink email={site.emails.support} /> if you think your account
      has been accessed without permission.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="responsibilities">4. Your responsibilities and permissions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Connect only Pages and accounts you are authorised to manage.</li>
    <li>
      Tell your customers how you handle their messages, including that you use {site.brand} and AI
      assistance, as your local law requires.
    </li>
    <li>Make sure the content in your knowledge base is accurate and that you may use it.</li>
    <li>Comply with the laws that apply to your business and your customer communications.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">5. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You must not use {site.brand} to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>send spam, unsolicited marketing or messages outside the rules Meta sets for messaging;</li>
    <li>send unlawful, harmful, deceptive, harassing or discriminatory content;</li>
    <li>collect sensitive data you are not allowed to collect;</li>
    <li>try to break, overload, reverse-engineer or get around the security of the service;</li>
    <li>resell or give access to the service to others without our written agreement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="meta">6. Facebook and Instagram integration terms</h2>
  <p>
    The integrations rely on Meta’s platforms. When you connect a Page or account, you must also
    follow Meta’s terms and policies, including its rules for business messaging. Meta may change or
    limit its platforms, which can affect what {site.brand} can do. {site.brand} is not affiliated
    with or endorsed by Meta.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can disconnect at any time inside {site.brand} or in your Facebook or Instagram settings.
    See the <a href="/integrations/facebook">Messenger</a> and{' '}
    <a href="/integrations/instagram">Instagram</a> integration pages.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">7. AI-generated responses and their limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      AI replies are generated automatically from your knowledge base and the conversation. They can
      be incomplete, out of date or wrong.
    </li>
    <li>
      You choose whether replies are sent automatically or reviewed first, and you are responsible
      for replies sent from your account.
    </li>
    <li>
      Do not rely on AI replies for legal, medical, financial or safety-critical advice to your
      customers.
    </li>
    <li>Hand conversations to a person whenever a customer needs one.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="payment">8. Payment, renewal, cancellation and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    <Fact fact={site.legal.pricingAndRefunds} />
  </p>

  <h2 id="availability">9. Availability and maintenance</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep {site.brand} running, but we do not promise it will be available without
    interruption. We may carry out maintenance, and features that depend on Meta may stop working if
    Meta changes or restricts its platforms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ip">10. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    We own {site.brand}, its software and its brand. You keep ownership of your content. You give us
    the permission we need to host, process and display your content only to provide the service to
    you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="data">11. Confidentiality and customer data ownership</h2>
  <p>
    Your conversation data and knowledge base belong to you. We process them on your instructions as
    described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, and we keep them confidential except
    where the law requires disclosure.
  </p>

  <h2 id="termination">12. Suspension, termination and data export</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can stop using {site.brand} and close your account at any time.</li>
    <li>
      We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms or Meta’s policies, or that puts
      the service or other users at risk. Where reasonable we will tell you first.
    </li>
    <li>
      Before closing your account you can ask for an export of your data by emailing{' '}
      <EmailLink email={site.emails.support} />. After closure, data is deleted as described on the{' '}
      <a href="/data-deletion">data deletion page</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="liability">13. Liability and governing law</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, for lost
    profits or data, or for problems caused by Meta’s platforms or by AI replies you chose to send.
    Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>
  <p>
    Liability cap:{' '}
    <Fact
      fact={{
        value: null,
        need: 'liability cap, if any (for example fees paid in the last 12 months)',
      }}
    />
  </p>
  <p>
    Governing law and courts: <Fact fact={site.legal.governingLaw} />
  </p>

  <h2 id="complaints">14. Complaints and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a complaint, email <EmailLink email={site.emails.support} /> and we will try to
    resolve it with you first.
  </p>
  <p>
    <Fact fact={site.legal.complaints} />
  </p>
</DocLayout>
